    "summary": "The count-table row label is derived by string-surgery on the section heading (`g.split(' (')[0]`) instead of storing a short label alongside the heading.",
    "failure_scenario": "Works only because exactly one of the three headings happens to contain a parenthetical to strip; if a future contributor renames the live-probe heading to omit the paren, or adds a fourth group whose heading contains an unrelated '(' earlier in the string (e.g. one describing a sub-condition), the summary-table row silently gets truncated to the wrong text with no error. A `{short_label: (heading, names)}` structure (or a list of `(short, heading, names)` tuples) makes the two strings independently correct by construction instead of one being parsed out of the other."
  },
