    "file": "backend/scripts/export_docs_reference.py",
    "line": 66,
    "summary": "`is_read` classifies a tool as read-only by pattern-matching the gate string (`startswith(\"read\")` or `endswith(\":view\")`) rather than from an explicit per-gate classification, while `LIVE_PROBE_TOOLS` right next to it IS an explicit hardcoded set — two different classification strategies for what is conceptually the same three-way split.",
    "failure_scenario": "A future gate value that is read-only but doesn't fit either string shape (e.g. a hypothetical `asset:view-summary` or `read-cached`) would silently land in \"Changes state\" with no test or `SystemExit` catching it (only `unknown_gates` against `GATE_LABEL` is checked, not against `is_read`'s pattern). Adding a `CATEGORY: dict[str, Literal[\"read\",\"write\"]]` beside `GATE_LABEL` — checked the same way unknown gates already are — removes the heuristic and the failure mode at once."
  }
